    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0124" n="108" sameAs="frus:frus1948v09/pg108"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.00/6–348: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">III. PARAGUAY</seg>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-06-03">June 3, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>263. President Morinigo<anchor n="1" xml:id="d83-f1"/> resigned at 0030 on demand
                    of Felipe <pb facs="0125" n="109" xml:id="pg109"/> Molas Lopez<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d83-f2"/> and Mario Mallorquin<anchor n="3" xml:id="d83-f3"/>
                    representing the civil forces of the revolution and in obedience to instruction
                    from Colonel Montanaro, Military Commander<anchor n="4" xml:id="d83-f4"/> of the
                    revolt. President Supreme Court Juan Manuel Frutos takes oath this morning as
                    Provisional President.…</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d83-f1" n="1" xml:id="d83-f1-content">
                <p>Gen. Higinio Morinigo.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d83-f2" n="2" xml:id="d83-f2-content">
                <p>Interventor of the National University.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d83-f3" n="3" xml:id="d83-f3-content">
                <p>Director of Lands and Colonization.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d83-f4" n="4" xml:id="d83-f4-content">
                <p>Col. Carlos Montanaro, Asunción garrison commander. Other leaders of the
                    police–army coup were Chief of Police Liberto Rodríguez, Maj. Adalberto Canata,
                    Commander of one of the Cavalry Regiments, and Abel Dos Santos, Mayor of
                    Asunción. (Despatch 297, June 15, from Asunción, 834.00/6–1548.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
